source_proof = "The pytest module executes the real generator against the current page tree, persists and reads its JSON transport, and asserts the inventory consumer contract: exact sorted page coverage, ten valid journeys, six original checks, synthetic-only accounts, observed=false and pending browser/manual AT status. Baseline digests prove all retained rows and journey/AT metadata are preserved. Read-only checks detect stale inventory; regeneration repairs missing routes; invalid evidence, duplicate rows and missing/empty source trees fail before writes."
review_only = "Browser execution, axe results, keyboard/focus behavior and manual NVDA/VoiceOver observations are not executed or qualified by this task. The existing mobile/corpus.test.mjs consumer is reviewed; its JSON assertions are exercised in Python without claiming a JavaScript run. journeys.ts remains unchanged and still requires actual browser/manual AT artifacts. No shell script, service unit, manifest or build file is repaired. This config-drift repair changes no runtime interface or restart-recovery component."
baseline = "Initial git status/diff showed only inherited .cgignore and spec task-status bookkeeping; the scoped repair record and pytest module were absent. The gate configuration reported zero build/verify runs and no gate ledger existed. No pre-change verification was run and no pre-change test failure is claimed: the explicit implementation-first order and hf-done-only verification rule supersede the contradictory baseline instruction. Static inspection found the removed source root and 14 uncovered current pages."
